WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.314 --> 00:00:02.773
- Maybe there's more to learn,
maybe there's a next step.

00:00:02.773 --> 00:00:05.216
If I could start from a
blank slate what would I do?

00:00:05.216 --> 00:00:07.689
I'd say, start quick and dirty.

00:00:07.689 --> 00:00:09.962
To let go of commitments
and say no to things.

00:00:09.962 --> 00:00:11.480
I'm now where I'm like,

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.613
would get a pie in my face
if I didn't stick to it.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.116
That could help us get through that dip.

00:00:15.116 --> 00:00:17.181
Even if you dive off that
cliff, you're going to be okay.

00:00:17.181 --> 00:00:18.992
Don't keep doing the same
thing over and over, right?

00:00:18.992 --> 00:00:21.697
Having that trust, you can't buy that.

00:00:21.697 --> 00:00:24.429
You become addicted that's your dopamine.

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:27.322
- He's a blogger, journalist
and published author.

00:00:27.322 --> 00:00:29.646
He's the creator of a
blog called Zen Habits.

00:00:29.646 --> 00:00:32.988
Time Magazine names Zen
Habits at the top of its list

00:00:32.988 --> 00:00:35.321
of the Top 25 Blogs in 2010.

00:00:36.864 --> 00:00:40.484
He's Leo Babauta, and here are
his Top 10 Rules for Success.

00:00:40.484 --> 00:00:43.897
(firework whooshing)

00:00:43.897 --> 00:00:46.117
- So actually, I had someone on Twitter,

00:00:46.117 --> 00:00:48.724
I ask people, like what's the one change

00:00:48.724 --> 00:00:50.029
that has helped you the most?

00:00:50.029 --> 00:00:52.445
And one person's, I really
loved his philosophy

00:00:52.445 --> 00:00:53.747
because it matches up with mine,

00:00:53.747 --> 00:00:58.403
which is that, he replaced
opinions with curiosity.

00:00:58.403 --> 00:01:00.184
And I love that because, to me,

00:01:00.184 --> 00:01:02.343
a lot of people get to this point where

00:01:02.343 --> 00:01:03.816
they think they know something.

00:01:03.816 --> 00:01:05.902
And when you think you know something,

00:01:05.902 --> 00:01:08.164
that's when learning ends.
- Right, you're done.

00:01:08.164 --> 00:01:09.138
- You're done.

00:01:09.138 --> 00:01:11.299
But if you just think,
I might know something

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:13.316
but let's find out more, maybe it's wrong.

00:01:13.316 --> 00:01:14.864
Maybe there's more to learn,

00:01:14.864 --> 00:01:17.435
maybe there's a next step.

00:01:17.435 --> 00:01:20.053
And there always is more to learn.

00:01:20.053 --> 00:01:23.022
So that's, to me, if you
just start with curiosity

00:01:23.022 --> 00:01:26.355
rather than, I think I know
it or I don't need to know it,

00:01:26.355 --> 00:01:28.550
or there's no way I'm going to know it,

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.394
that's a much better place
to start, and it's fun.

00:01:31.394 --> 00:01:34.966
Like, learning new things
and trying new things.

00:01:34.966 --> 00:01:38.798
It's really important
to look at your habits

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:42.113
if you're a new entrepreneur
or been doing it for awhile,

00:01:42.113 --> 00:01:46.280
I think we tend to fall
into these routines, right?

00:01:48.235 --> 00:01:50.981
And that routine is a lot of times

00:01:50.981 --> 00:01:52.873
if you don't know
consciously, it's a routine

00:01:52.873 --> 00:01:55.835
that just happens to build up over time.

00:01:55.835 --> 00:01:59.304
So like, you might be busy
checking Facebook and Twitter,

00:01:59.304 --> 00:02:01.718
and all your stats and everything else

00:02:01.718 --> 00:02:04.212
and so that you develop this routine

00:02:04.212 --> 00:02:07.795
of quickly checking
through everything online.

00:02:07.795 --> 00:02:11.783
And what that means is,
that's just through,

00:02:11.783 --> 00:02:13.881
just through building that up over time,

00:02:13.881 --> 00:02:16.767
that routine of checking everything.

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:19.317
And what that means is
that you don't have time

00:02:19.317 --> 00:02:21.757
for the creation, the part that I think,

00:02:21.757 --> 00:02:23.900
for me at least is really important.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.169
And so, I think it's good
to sometimes just step back,

00:02:27.169 --> 00:02:29.595
and take a look at what habits
you've created over time.

00:02:29.595 --> 00:02:32.817
And say, what can I do more consciously?

00:02:32.817 --> 00:02:35.493
If I could start from a
blank slate, what would I do?

00:02:35.493 --> 00:02:39.388
And start to change those,
to build those consciously.

00:02:39.388 --> 00:02:42.063
But what I found, though, is that,

00:02:42.063 --> 00:02:44.164
a lot of times what we
do is we try to implement

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.751
an entire system, of habits all at once,

00:02:46.751 --> 00:02:48.389
this new thing that we read about,

00:02:48.389 --> 00:02:51.341
and it collapses after a little while.

00:02:51.341 --> 00:02:53.363
We go back into our old habits.

00:02:53.363 --> 00:02:55.449
And one of the problems with that,

00:02:55.449 --> 00:02:59.616
is that we're implementing a
whole series of habits at once.

00:03:00.718 --> 00:03:03.446
And again, if you start
a new morning routine,

00:03:03.446 --> 00:03:05.941
you might actually be doing
5-10 different habits,

00:03:05.941 --> 00:03:07.719
one right after the other,

00:03:07.719 --> 00:03:12.136
and so you're chaining them
together, a bunch of new habits,

00:03:12.136 --> 00:03:13.957
and that's great for like a week or so,

00:03:13.957 --> 00:03:15.841
and then it collapses.

00:03:15.841 --> 00:03:17.210
And I've seen that so many times,

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.127
I've done it myself plenty of times,

00:03:19.127 --> 00:03:22.461
and what I found is that doesn't,
that's not very effective.

00:03:22.461 --> 00:03:23.868
Some people can make it work

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.549
but most people are not
going to succeed at that.

00:03:25.549 --> 00:03:27.014
So what you really want to do is

00:03:27.014 --> 00:03:28.809
keep doing what you've been doing

00:03:28.809 --> 00:03:31.993
that's going to keep the boat afloat,

00:03:31.993 --> 00:03:34.111
but if you wanted to
start to make changes,

00:03:34.111 --> 00:03:36.129
start making little changes one at a time.

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:38.599
To get going, a lot of people are afraid

00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:40.958
to just get started, they
want to have it perfect,

00:03:40.958 --> 00:03:42.856
perfect design and everything like that.

00:03:42.856 --> 00:03:45.189
I'd say, start quick and dirty.

00:03:45.189 --> 00:03:48.001
Just start, start writing posts,

00:03:48.001 --> 00:03:51.623
and the posts be as useful as possible.

00:03:51.623 --> 00:03:54.799
And think about what your
readers' problems are,

00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:56.795
and help them solve those problems.

00:03:56.795 --> 00:03:59.350
So, don't let that kind of fear

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:01.747
of getting started stop you, just start.

00:04:01.747 --> 00:04:03.927
We all have the same
amount of time in the day,

00:04:03.927 --> 00:04:06.542
but it's just, we have filled the day up

00:04:06.542 --> 00:04:09.548
with all these things that
we think we need to do,

00:04:09.548 --> 00:04:10.965
like commitments.

00:04:12.116 --> 00:04:15.059
One thing, I was coaching soccer,

00:04:15.059 --> 00:04:17.878
because I thought that
was important for my kids.

00:04:17.878 --> 00:04:22.551
I was on the board of the
PTO at my kid's school,

00:04:22.551 --> 00:04:24.275
because I thought that was important.

00:04:24.275 --> 00:04:27.134
But I realized that I was
spending time doing stuff

00:04:27.134 --> 00:04:30.491
with other people instead
of the actual kids.

00:04:30.491 --> 00:04:33.280
So I realized if I let
go of those commitments,

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.693
even though I thought they were important,

00:04:34.693 --> 00:04:36.922
I have time then to
actually spend with people

00:04:36.922 --> 00:04:38.171
who are important to me.

00:04:38.171 --> 00:04:40.061
So you learn to let go of commitments

00:04:40.061 --> 00:04:42.754
and say no to things,
so that you can say yes

00:04:42.754 --> 00:04:44.267
to the things you really want,

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:45.705
that are really important to you.

00:04:45.705 --> 00:04:48.095
So I've had to, I mean,
sometimes it's simple as like,

00:04:48.095 --> 00:04:50.918
an email saying I can't do this anymore.

00:04:50.918 --> 00:04:52.178
I don't have the time.

00:04:52.178 --> 00:04:54.202
And you feel like you're
going to disappoint people

00:04:54.202 --> 00:04:55.713
so you don't want to say no to them,

00:04:55.713 --> 00:04:57.727
but you know what I learned,

00:04:57.727 --> 00:04:59.826
life goes on, they figure it out.

00:04:59.826 --> 00:05:03.492
If you have a group
around this habit change,

00:05:03.492 --> 00:05:07.775
all of a sudden, you now have
a whole different environment

00:05:07.775 --> 00:05:10.998
that gives you a
different feedback system.

00:05:10.998 --> 00:05:13.776
So, if you're going to, if you
say, if you tell your group,

00:05:13.776 --> 00:05:15.608
and this has to be a group of people

00:05:15.608 --> 00:05:17.217
that you actually care
about their opinion,

00:05:17.217 --> 00:05:18.705
because otherwise you'll
just forget about it.

00:05:18.705 --> 00:05:20.238
But if you care about their opinion,

00:05:20.238 --> 00:05:22.399
and let's say it's 5-10 people,

00:05:22.399 --> 00:05:26.690
and you say, I am going to write every day

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:31.006
before I check email, or
I pay you $10,000, right?

00:05:31.006 --> 00:05:34.334
If you told people that,
you would definitely do it.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:37.145
Or, you know, I've done
one where I've like,

00:05:37.145 --> 00:05:39.657
would get a pie in my face
if I didn't stick to it,

00:05:39.657 --> 00:05:41.737
things like that, or I'd donate to

00:05:41.737 --> 00:05:44.252
the political party you don't like.

00:05:44.252 --> 00:05:46.015
- Or you're going to have to eat

00:05:46.015 --> 00:05:47.621
some factory-farmed meat or something.

00:05:47.621 --> 00:05:48.454
- Exactly.

00:05:48.454 --> 00:05:50.994
Something you definitely
do not want to do.

00:05:50.994 --> 00:05:52.904
Actually I went up for my book.

00:05:52.904 --> 00:05:54.739
You know, I'm a vegan.

00:05:54.739 --> 00:05:56.227
I promised you and some other friends

00:05:56.227 --> 00:05:58.810
that I would eat a beef burger,

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:04.138
not just a veggie burger if
I didn't have this book done

00:06:04.138 --> 00:06:05.362
by the end of the year.

00:06:05.362 --> 00:06:07.694
And so I was motivated to
get up and start writing.

00:06:07.694 --> 00:06:09.626
But anyway, commit to this group,

00:06:09.626 --> 00:06:14.406
create a consequence that you
definitely are not going to...

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:17.263
you don't want to have, and you're
definitely not going to fail.

00:06:17.263 --> 00:06:19.176
And so when you do the habit,

00:06:19.176 --> 00:06:21.956
you get the positive benefit

00:06:21.956 --> 00:06:23.749
of getting to report back to them.

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:25.469
And even as you do the
habit, you're thinking,

00:06:25.469 --> 00:06:27.392
oh, I get to tell Corbett
that I'm going to do this,

00:06:27.392 --> 00:06:28.649
or that I did this.

00:06:28.649 --> 00:06:30.572
And so that's positive
feedback for doing it,

00:06:30.572 --> 00:06:32.664
and if you didn't do it,
you have negative feedback

00:06:32.664 --> 00:06:35.023
and have to tell your group
that "I didn't do it."

00:06:35.023 --> 00:06:35.985
And that would be shameful,

00:06:35.985 --> 00:06:38.839
and you don't want to look
bad in the eyes of your peers.

00:06:38.839 --> 00:06:40.988
And you probably have to,
you know, eat the burger

00:06:40.988 --> 00:06:43.092
or get the pie in the face.

00:06:43.092 --> 00:06:44.430
And so you wouldn't want to do that.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:46.361
So now you've just
reversed the feedback loop

00:06:46.361 --> 00:06:49.454
with that very simple
change in your environment.

00:06:49.454 --> 00:06:53.347
So I think, a lot of times
we have a dip in motivation,

00:06:53.347 --> 00:06:55.300
and if we have a purpose,

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.533
that can help us get through that dip.

00:06:57.533 --> 00:07:01.061
And it also helps guide us as we like,

00:07:01.061 --> 00:07:03.377
'cause there's tons of
decisions that we have to make

00:07:03.377 --> 00:07:06.744
on a daily basis and over the long term,

00:07:06.744 --> 00:07:09.089
and if you have some kind of purpose,

00:07:09.089 --> 00:07:12.378
that kind of gives you a
little bit of a compass.

00:07:12.378 --> 00:07:16.523
And that has helped me
tremendously in the last,

00:07:16.523 --> 00:07:19.151
I think, seven, eight years
since I've been doing this.

00:07:19.151 --> 00:07:21.000
Even if you're just starting out,

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.914
you haven't gone to that
place where you're like

00:07:22.914 --> 00:07:25.143
all confident, you're in
this place where you're like,

00:07:25.143 --> 00:07:27.217
you're in this little comfort zone,

00:07:27.217 --> 00:07:30.796
you know what you're doing, and
you don't want to venture out.

00:07:30.796 --> 00:07:33.037
Or maybe you've gotten that confidence,

00:07:33.037 --> 00:07:35.932
and you hit that cliff or that door

00:07:35.932 --> 00:07:37.462
that's like really scary,

00:07:37.462 --> 00:07:38.641
and what do you do then?

00:07:38.641 --> 00:07:40.098
And what you've developed,

00:07:40.098 --> 00:07:41.520
and I think what I've developed too,

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.237
it's just, it's not a confidence
that I know everything,

00:07:44.237 --> 00:07:47.519
but a confidence that even
if you dive off that cliff,

00:07:47.519 --> 00:07:48.839
you're going to be okay.

00:07:48.839 --> 00:07:51.833
And that's, I think that's
really the crucial thing,

00:07:51.833 --> 00:07:54.544
is learning, it doesn't matter if I fail,

00:07:54.544 --> 00:07:56.454
it doesn't matter if
I don't know anything,

00:07:56.454 --> 00:07:59.562
it doesn't matter if I
stumble around in the darkness

00:07:59.562 --> 00:08:01.265
not knowing what I'm doing.

00:08:01.265 --> 00:08:02.870
I'll be okay.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.583
And there's really, that's
the confidence that you need.

00:08:05.583 --> 00:08:08.185
You know my story back in 2005

00:08:08.185 --> 00:08:10.257
when I was stuck with
all these bad habits,

00:08:10.257 --> 00:08:11.789
and I couldn't make any changes.

00:08:11.789 --> 00:08:14.162
I kept trying to change them all at once.

00:08:14.162 --> 00:08:15.658
I would change my entire diet,

00:08:15.658 --> 00:08:18.129
which, you know, diet is
actually a series of habits.

00:08:18.129 --> 00:08:21.281
I would change my entire exercise routine,

00:08:21.281 --> 00:08:23.892
I would try and quit smoking,
try and be productive

00:08:23.892 --> 00:08:25.996
and stop procrastinating, wake up early.

00:08:25.996 --> 00:08:28.120
And I would do all of these at once.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:30.151
And I kept failing, I
couldn't understand why.

00:08:30.151 --> 00:08:32.873
It wasn't really that it was me,

00:08:32.873 --> 00:08:34.979
a lot of times I would internalize it.

00:08:34.979 --> 00:08:36.485
Actually all the time
I would internalize it

00:08:36.485 --> 00:08:39.154
and think, I have no
self-control, I'm not disciplined,

00:08:39.154 --> 00:08:41.844
I'm not good enough, I'm
not strong, I'm just weak.

00:08:41.844 --> 00:08:43.399
And so I would feel bad about myself

00:08:43.399 --> 00:08:45.169
and develop this negative self-image,

00:08:45.169 --> 00:08:48.927
and basically destroyed any
trust that I had in myself.

00:08:48.927 --> 00:08:51.096
But really it wasn't a problem with me,

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:52.714
it was a problem with the method.

00:08:52.714 --> 00:08:55.119
And so what I'm proposing is,

00:08:55.119 --> 00:08:57.118
instead of failing over and over

00:08:57.118 --> 00:08:59.066
at creating a whole
bunch of habits at once,

00:08:59.066 --> 00:09:01.602
or one really big habit
instead of a small one,

00:09:01.602 --> 00:09:03.362
instead of failing at that,

00:09:03.362 --> 00:09:06.362
change the method and if you failed,

00:09:07.953 --> 00:09:10.089
don't keep doing the same
thing over and over, right?

00:09:10.089 --> 00:09:12.107
You got to make some changes.

00:09:12.107 --> 00:09:16.885
So what I'm proposing is,
take that failure as a lesson

00:09:16.885 --> 00:09:20.365
and adapt your habit
change and be smarter.

00:09:20.365 --> 00:09:21.966
Do it in a smarter way.

00:09:21.966 --> 00:09:24.516
This public image that we try and create

00:09:24.516 --> 00:09:26.817
either for ourselves or for our business,

00:09:26.817 --> 00:09:29.832
I mean it's not real, first of all.

00:09:29.832 --> 00:09:33.884
And second of all, if you
let that image crumble

00:09:33.884 --> 00:09:35.956
and have cracks and stuff

00:09:35.956 --> 00:09:39.387
and show the honest reality
of things, people like that.

00:09:39.387 --> 00:09:40.802
- I agree, yeah.

00:09:40.802 --> 00:09:44.033
- And they start to trust
you because you're honest.

00:09:44.033 --> 00:09:46.423
And what you and I know is that,

00:09:46.423 --> 00:09:49.186
that trust is more valuable
than anything else.

00:09:49.186 --> 00:09:51.957
It's more valuable than
getting a click to subscribe

00:09:51.957 --> 00:09:53.537
or share or buy.

00:09:53.537 --> 00:09:56.674
Having that trust, you can't buy that.

00:09:56.674 --> 00:09:59.539
And the only thing you
can do is be trustworthy,

00:09:59.539 --> 00:10:02.129
and be honest and be real.

00:10:02.129 --> 00:10:04.379
And if you have this veneer

00:10:05.819 --> 00:10:07.207
of this public image that you have,

00:10:07.207 --> 00:10:09.120
I'm preaching to the choir here,

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.800
but I'm hoping other people will hear it.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:14.050
That is fake and people can sense that.

00:10:15.186 --> 00:10:18.174
People have intuition about
whether this person is just

00:10:18.174 --> 00:10:19.916
giving you a marketing pitch,

00:10:19.916 --> 00:10:22.181
or if they're giving you the real deal.

00:10:22.181 --> 00:10:24.054
And if you give them the real deal,

00:10:24.054 --> 00:10:26.892
they start to trust you because
they know you're sincere,

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:30.392
you're not just trying to get their money,

00:10:30.392 --> 00:10:33.137
which most people are trying to do online.

00:10:33.137 --> 00:10:35.354
And if you are one of the few who aren't,

00:10:35.354 --> 00:10:39.231
you've set yourself apart as
trustworthy, honest, sincere,

00:10:39.231 --> 00:10:43.564
and someone who is there
to genuinely help them

00:10:43.564 --> 00:10:44.731
rather than...

00:11:17.327 --> 00:11:20.979
You just, you become addicted,
that's your dopamine.

00:11:20.979 --> 00:11:25.069
And so I'm totally
addicted to helping people

00:11:25.069 --> 00:11:27.847
change their lives through
habits, through mindfulness,

00:11:27.847 --> 00:11:30.161
and all these other things
that I've been working on.

00:11:30.161 --> 00:11:34.328
But I don't think that I have
done all my work on that yet.

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.022
I think there's a lot that I have to learn

00:11:38.022 --> 00:11:39.108
about helping people.

00:11:39.108 --> 00:11:40.579
I think there's a lot of people out there

00:11:40.579 --> 00:11:41.841
who I haven't reached yet, and so

00:11:41.841 --> 00:11:43.696
that really is what gets
me up in the morning.

00:11:43.696 --> 00:11:45.295
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:11:45.295 --> 00:11:47.891
I made this video because
Harold Kuhn asked me to.

00:11:47.891 --> 00:11:49.733
